Track 2: Poste Restante, Longyearbyen
- Story & Context: Postal clerk Einar Vang sat beside an iron stove in Svalbard holding an uncollected dispatch from Bahia whose recipient had vanished during the first blizzard of November. Over the course of three sleepless days, Vang recorded the rhythmic clatter of his sorting stamp against the desk, syncing the clicks to the suspended, faint respiration of ground-squirrels sleeping deep beneath the coal mines. Between drafts of chicory brew, he whistled a skeletal samba into a reel-to-reel recorder, delivering a quiet, guilt-ridden confession about holding onto mail that wasn't his, murmuring at the fade: "nobody answers when the seals are broken."
